            <ArticleTitle>[The Tolosa-Hunt syndrome. Case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>355-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of headaches with recurrent paralysis of cranial nerves III, IV, V and VI is reported. A good therapeutic effect was obtained with corticoids. After ruling out other diseases and causes of ophthalmoplegia the Tolosa-Hunt syndrome was diagnosed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
